#. Tag: title
#: functions.docbook:53
#, no-c-format
msgid "BITLSHIFT"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: functions.docbook:54
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The BITLSHIFT() function performs a bit-wise left shift operation of the "
"first parameter. The number of bits to shift by is specified by the second "
"parameter. Note that a negative number of bits to left shift by becomes a "
"right shift."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: functions.docbook:59
#, no-c-format
msgid "BITLSHIFT(value; shift size)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: seg
#: functions.docbook:64
#, no-c-format
msgid "Amount to left shift by"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: member
#: functions.docbook:67 functions.docbook:87
#, no-c-format
msgid "<link linkend=\"BITLSHIFT\">BITLSHIFT</link>&nbsp;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: functions.docbook:73
#, no-c-format
msgid "BITRSHIFT"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: functions.docbook:74
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The BITRSHIFT() function performs a bit-wise right shift operation of the "
"first parameter. The number of bits to shift by is specified by the second "
"parameter. Note that a negative number of bits to right shift by becomes a "
"left shift."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: functions.docbook:79
#, no-c-format
msgid "BITRSHIFT(value; shift size)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: seg
#: functions.docbook:84
#, no-c-format
msgid "Amount to right shift by"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: functions.docbook:93
#, no-c-format
msgid "BITOR"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: functions.docbook:94
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The BITOR() function performs a bit-wise OR operation for the two integer "
"parameters."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: functions.docbook:99
#, no-c-format
msgid "BITOR(value; value)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: functions.docbook:107
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"BITOR(12;10) returns 14 (because decimal 12 is binary 1100, and decimal 10 "
"is binary 1010; and 1100 \"ored\" with 1010 is 1110, which is integer 14)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: member
#: functions.docbook:110 functions.docbook:133
#, no-c-format
msgid "<link linkend=\"BITAND\">BITAND</link>&nbsp;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: functions.docbook:116
#, no-c-format
msgid "BITXOR"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: functions.docbook:117
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The BITXOR() function performs a bit-wise exclusive-OR operation for the two "
"integer parameters."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: functions.docbook:122
#, no-c-format
msgid "BITXOR(value; value)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: functions.docbook:130
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"BITXOR(12;10) returns 6 (because decimal 12 is binary 1100, and decimal 10 "
"is binary 1010; and 1100 \"xored\" with 1010 is 0110, which is integer 6)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: functions.docbook:139
#, no-c-format
msgid "Engineering"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: functions.docbook:142
#, no-c-format
msgid "BASE"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: functions.docbook:143
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The BASE() function converts a number from base-10 to a string value in a "
"target base from 2 to 36."
msgstr ""

